    <system:String x:Key="setup_wizard_title">Getting started</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_welcome_title">Welcome to Songify</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_welcome_body">This short guide links your music source, optional Twitch song requests, and a stream overlay (text file or widget). Skip anything and change it later in Settings or from Home.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_player_title">Which player do you use?</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_player_body">Most people use Spotify. You can switch this later from the Home screen.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_title">Connect Spotify</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_body">Create a Spotify Developer app, paste the Client ID here, then link your account. The help button opens the setup guide.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_help_tooltip">Open the Spotify setup guide</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_open_guide">How to get a Client ID</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_linked">Linked as {0}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_linked_unknown">Linked</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_spotify_not_linked">Not linked yet. You can do this later in Settings.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_twitch_title">Connect Twitch</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_twitch_body">Link your broadcaster account if you want song requests in chat. Skip this if you only need a now-playing overlay. A bot account can be added later in Settings.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_twitch_linked">Linked as {0}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_twitch_linked_unknown">Twitch account linked.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_twitch_not_linked">Optional if you only need a now-playing overlay.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_title">Song requests</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_body">Viewers can request songs with channel points, chat commands, or both. Skip this if you only want a now-playing overlay.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_reward">Channel points</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_reward_hint">Viewers redeem a reward to request a song. Next you can create a reward or pick an existing one. Refunds only work for rewards created in Songify.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_command">Chat commands</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_command_hint">Viewers type !ssr plus a song name. This enables the song request command. Edit the trigger, user levels, and replies later in Settings → Commands. Connect the bot from the Twitch status icon when you go live.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_create_reward">Create reward</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_open_rewards">Open reward settings</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_open_commands">Open command settings</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_requests_need_twitch">Link Twitch first to create a reward or enable chat commands.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_title">Choose song request rewards</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_body">Check every channel-point reward that should add a song. You can assign skip or skip-poll rewards later in Settings → Rewards.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_refund">Automatic refunds only work when Songify created the reward. Rewards made in the Twitch dashboard cannot be refunded from here. Songify-created rewards show the Songify icon.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_loading">Loading rewards…</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_empty">No rewards yet. Create one below, or make one on Twitch and tap Refresh.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_error">Could not load rewards. Link Twitch and try Refresh.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_refresh">Refresh</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_manageable">Refunds work (created in Songify)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_rewards_selected">{0} selected for song requests</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_limits_title">Request rules</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_limits_body">Set who may request via channel points and how many songs they can have in the queue. You can change all of this later without running setup again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_limits_who">Who can request with channel points</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_limits_who_hint">Subscriber tiers and more options are in Settings → Song requests.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_limits_queue">Max songs in queue (per user)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_limits_queue_hint">Applies to every user level for now. Settings → Song requests lets you set a different limit per badge, plus cooldowns.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_later_title">Where to adjust this later</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_later_song_requests">Settings → Song requests — who can request, queue limits, cooldowns.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_later_rewards">Settings → Rewards — pick rewards, skip rewards, and refund conditions.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_later_commands">Settings → Commands — enable !ssr and other chat commands, triggers, and who may use them.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_later_responses">Settings → Responses — what the bot says in chat.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_title">Stream widget</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_body">A browser widget shows the current song in OBS with more style options than a text file. Hosted widgets (including Premium ones) live on songify.rocks. Skip this if you only want Songify.txt.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_use">Use a widget overlay</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_use_hint">Turns on song upload so hosted widgets can follow what is playing. You can change this later in Settings → Output.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_gallery">Browse widgets</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_gallery_hint">Full gallery, including Premium widgets. Copy a URL into an OBS Browser source.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_generator">Widget generator</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_generator_hint">Simple customizer for a basic now-playing bar.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_local">Local overlay (web server)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_local_hint">For custom HTML overlays and the JSON API. Start the server, then open the local page.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_open_local">Open local page</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_widget_port">Web server port</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_output_title">Song output file</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_output_body">Songify writes the current song to this text file. In OBS, add a Text source and point it at Songify.txt.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_done_title">You're ready</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_done_body">Anything still open can be finished from Home or Settings. Use Show me around to see Song requests, Rewards, and widgets in the app.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_skip">Skip</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_back">Back</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_next">Next</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_finish">Finish</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_show_me_around">Show me around</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_step_label">Step {0} of {1}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_title">Getting started</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_body">Finish these so Songify can show the current song, take requests, and drive your overlay.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_dismiss">Dismiss</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_go">Go</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_spotify">Link Spotify</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_twitch">Link Twitch (for song requests)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_output">Song output file (OBS)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_token">Add Songify API token</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_requests">Choose channel points or chat commands</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_reward">Pick a song request reward</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_checklist_widget">Set up a stream widget</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_token_title">Songify API token</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_token_body">Web services such as uploading the current song and the request queue need a Songify API token. Log in on songify.rocks with your Twitch account, generate a token on your account page, then paste it here. If the website offers Import to Songify, that sends the token to this app automatically.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_token_get">Get token</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_token_missing">No token yet. Song data and queue uploads will not work until you add one.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="setup_token_present">Token saved. Generate a new one on your account page if you need to replace it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_settings_songify_api_token_help">Required for web song data and the request queue. Log in on songify.rocks with Twitch, generate a token on your account page, then paste it here or use Import to Songify on the website.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_overview_api_token_title">Songify API token required</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_overview_api_token_body">Song data and the request queue will not update on the web until you add a Songify API token. Log in on songify.rocks with Twitch, generate a token on your account page, then import it in Settings → Config.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_console_detach">Detach</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_console_open_window">Console window</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_console_detached_title">Console is in another window</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_console_detached_body">The log is open in a separate window so you can watch it while you use the rest of Songify. Close that window to bring the console back here.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="window_console_show_window">Show window</system:String>
